-- Replace only the bundled English About placeholder; preserve editorial overrides and metadata.
UPDATE `aowow_articles`
SET `article` = '[h2]A reference for Wrath of the Lich King[/h2]\n[b]AoWoW is a community-developed database website for World of Warcraft: Wrath of the Lich King, focused on version 3.3.5, build 12340.[/b] It turns game records into searchable pages that help players understand items, quests, spells, creatures and the world around them. Whether you are planning a character, checking a quest requirement or looking for a crafting material, AoWoW brings the relevant information together and connects it to related records.\n\nThe application can be run by individual server communities using their own configured game data. Its familiar database layout makes it easy to move from a name or an ID to the details behind it, then follow the links to rewards, locations, abilities and other useful context.\n\n[h2]Explore the database[/h2]\nStart with the search box when you know a name. Browse a category when you want to compare possibilities or discover related content. These are some useful starting points:\n\n[table class=grid]\n[tr][td=header]Browse[/td][td=header]What you can discover[/td][/tr]\n[tr][td][url=?items]Items[/url] and [url=?spells]spells[/url][/td][td]Equipment, materials, recipes, abilities and their requirements. Follow related records to investigate how an item or effect fits into your plans.[/td][/tr]\n[tr][td][url=?quests]Quests[/url] and [url=?objects]objects[/url][/td][td]Objectives, rewards and the people or objects involved in a quest. Check the relevant entries before setting out.[/td][/tr]\n[tr][td][url=?npcs]NPCs[/url] and [url=?zones]zones[/url][/td][td]Creatures, bosses and places across the game world, with the location and encounter information available in the database.[/td][/tr]\n[tr][td][url=?talent]Talent calculator[/url] and [url=?maps]maps[/url][/td][td]Explore character builds and game locations. Talent-build links let you save a setup or share it with other players.[/td][/tr]\n[tr][td][url=?guides]Guides[/url] and [url=?events]events[/url][/td][td]Read published explanations and browse seasonal activities. Guides can bring several database entries together into a practical route or checklist.[/td][/tr]\n[/table]\n\n[h2]Where the information comes from[/h2]\nAoWoW combines information extracted from the Wrath game client with records imported from a configured game-world database. Client data supplies details such as names, icons, spell information and map resources. World data supplies relationships such as creature spawns, loot and quest connections. The project was developed around TrinityCore, and its setup prepares these sources for browsing on the web.\n\nThe records shown by an installation reflect the data its administrators have imported and maintained. Custom changes and differences between server databases can affect what appears on a page. When checking a requirement, drop or location, consider the game version and the particular server you play on.\n\n[h2]A project with a history[/h2]\nThe project\'s recorded history reaches back to releases in [b]2008[/b]. Its earliest creator is not identified in the project documentation. Later development rewrote the server-side PHP application and updated the older client-side JavaScript, continuing the idea of a browsable reference for a specific era of World of Warcraft.\n\nThat history explains AoWoW\'s focus on preserving useful Wrath-era information and the connections between individual game records. Continued work on imports, compatibility, security and presentation helps keep that reference usable. You can read the [url=https://github.com/Sarjuuk/aowow#introduction]project\'s historical introduction[/url] for the original account of its origins.\n\n[h2]Community knowledge and corrections[/h2]\nDatabase records provide the foundation; players add the context. Comments can explain a difficult objective, screenshots can clarify what to look for, and guides can connect a series of steps that would otherwise be spread across many pages. Useful contributions describe what happened, where it happened and which conditions mattered. The [url=?help=commenting-and-you]commenting guide[/url] explains how to make that information helpful to other readers.\n\nIf you find an incorrect entry or a broken link, use the [b]Feedback[/b] option in the page header. Include the affected page, the detail you believe is wrong and any evidence that helps explain the correction. Clear reports make it easier to distinguish a data error from a difference in game version or server behavior.\n\n[h2]Credits[/h2]\nThe project credits [b]mix[/b] for client-data and image parsers, [b]LordJZ[/b] for database and account foundations, [b]kliver[/b] for screenshot support, and [b]Sarjuuk[/b] for project maintenance. AoWoW also acknowledges the earlier database presentation and client scripting that influenced its interface, alongside the work of later contributors and community members.\n\nWorld of Warcraft and its game assets remain the property of Blizzard Entertainment and the applicable rights holders. Other third-party materials belong to their respective owners.'
WHERE `url` = 'aboutus' AND `locale` = 0 AND `rev` = 0 AND `editAccess` = 2
    AND `type` IS NULL AND `typeId` IS NULL
    AND SHA2(`article`, 256) = '0c213e3429f0a5ddfd7a6cb08b8dad1eed8a2855645c24f6f18c8b20463c34ca';

-- Replace only the bundled English FAQ placeholder, retaining editorial overrides.
UPDATE `aowow_articles`
SET `article` = 'Find practical answers about browsing the database, planning a character and contributing useful information. AoWoW focuses on [b]World of Warcraft: Wrath of the Lich King, version 3.3.5, build 12340[/b]. For the project\'s background, history and credits, visit [url=?aboutus]About AoWoW[/url].\n\n[h2]Useful help pages[/h2]\n[table class=grid]\n[tr][td=header]Topic[/td][td=header]Read more[/td][/tr]\n[tr][td]Comments and moderation[/td][td][url=?help=commenting-and-you]Commenting guide[/url][/td][/tr]\n[tr][td]Formatting and links[/td][td][url=?help=markup-guide]Markup guide[/url][/td][/tr]\n[tr][td]Talent builds[/td][td][url=?help=talent-calculator]Talent calculator help[/url][/td][/tr]\n[tr][td]Comparing equipment[/td][td][url=?help=item-comparison]Item comparison help[/url][/td][/tr]\n[tr][td]Gear scores and presets[/td][td][url=?help=stat-weighting]Stat-weighting help[/url][/td][/tr]\n[tr][td]Screenshots[/td][td][url=?help=screenshots-tips-tricks]Screenshot tips[/url][/td][/tr]\n[tr][td]Tooltips on another website[/td][td][url=?tooltips]Tooltip instructions[/url][/td][/tr]\n[/table]\n\n[h2]Getting started[/h2]\n[h3]What can I use AoWoW for?[/h3]\nUse it to look up items, quests, spells, NPCs and locations, then follow the connections between them. A quest page can lead to its rewards; an item page can help you investigate its sources. Calculators, maps and published guides provide additional ways to plan what to do next.\n\n[h3]Do I need an account to browse?[/h3]\nPublic database entries and help pages can be read without signing in. An account is needed for community actions such as posting comments or submitting screenshots, subject to the site\'s settings and your account permissions. Use the [url=?account=signin]sign-in page[/url] for the available login and recovery options.\n\n[h3]Will every detail match the server I play on?[/h3]\nThe entries reflect the game data imported by this installation. Custom server changes, database updates and expansion differences can affect requirements, loot and locations. Check the relevant version and conditions before assuming that information from another server applies here.\n\n[h2]Finding and understanding information[/h2]\n[h3]How do I find a specific entry?[/h3]\nEnter a name in the search box or browse the relevant database category. If you know a record\'s type and numeric ID, you can search for them together. For example:\n[code]item 49623[/code]\nThis opens that item directly. Including the type helps distinguish an item ID from a quest, spell or NPC with the same number.\n\n[h3]What should I check when I cannot find something?[/h3]\nTry a distinctive part of the name, check the spelling and confirm the selected language. When browsing a category, clear restrictive filters and check later result pages. Content from a different expansion or a custom server may be absent from this installation\'s data.\n\n[h3]What are the related tabs on an entry for?[/h3]\nThey organize information connected to the record, such as quest rewards, loot sources, abilities or related items. The available tabs depend on the entry and its data. When investigating a drop, read the source and difficulty information together; random loot can vary between individual kills.\n\n[h3]Why can a location or map pin differ from what I see in game?[/h3]\nMaps use the location data available to the website. Dungeon floors, quest conditions and server changes can affect where something appears. Select the appropriate floor and read any accompanying notes. A database pin describes a recorded location; it does not track an NPC\'s current movement in your game session.\n\n[h2]Tools and character planning[/h2]\n[h3]How do I save or share a talent build?[/h3]\nUse the [url=?talent]talent calculator[/url], then copy the address or use its build-link option. Open a shared local build link directly in your browser. The Import button accepts older Wrath-style URL formats; the talent calculator help explains those formats. You do not need to visit an external calculator to use an existing compatible link.\n\n[h3]How can I compare equipment?[/h3]\nUse item comparison to review the attributes of equipment together, and consult the comparison help for the available controls. Consider the item\'s requirements, slot and intended use alongside its stats. A larger value in one attribute may involve a trade-off elsewhere.\n\n[h3]Does a higher stat-weight score always mean an item is better?[/h3]\nA score follows the weights you have chosen. Presets are starting points, and their usefulness depends on your build, current equipment and goals. Adjust weights for your situation, including stats that have already reached a useful cap. Read the stat-weighting help before treating the score as a final decision.\n\n[h3]Can I add these tooltips to another website?[/h3]\nThe tooltip instructions explain how to load this installation\'s widget and attach game-record tooltips to links. They also cover supported options such as item level, enchants and gems. Follow the local examples so the widget requests data from the intended database.\n\n[h2]Contributions and feedback[/h2]\n[h3]How do I add a useful comment or screenshot?[/h3]\nSign in and use the contribution controls on the relevant entry, where available. Explain the specific objective, location or condition your contribution clarifies. Check existing comments first, and keep screenshots focused on useful game information. The commenting, markup and screenshot guides above provide practical guidance.\n\n[h3]Why might a comment be removed?[/h3]\nModeration follows the guidelines in the commenting help. Comments that do not meet those guidelines may be deleted. Keep your contribution relevant to the entry, distinguish what you observed from what you suspect, and correct or update information when it becomes misleading.\n\n[h3]How do I report incorrect information or a broken page?[/h3]\nUse the Feedback option in the page header or open [url=?aboutus#contact]our contact form[/url]. Include the affected URL or record ID, what you expected, what actually happened and any useful evidence. For game-data differences, mention the version, difficulty or quest conditions involved. Clear reports help identify the right correction.\n\n[h2]Using the website[/h2]\n[h3]Do I need JavaScript?[/h3]\nCore entry text and ordinary links are supplied as readable page content. Interactive features, including calculators, map controls, tooltips and advanced filtering, need JavaScript. If those controls fail to appear, check your browser\'s script settings and reload the page. You can still use the available text and links while investigating.\n\n[h3]Why is a tool, image or other feature unavailable?[/h3]\nAvailable features depend on the site\'s configuration and the data or assets it has prepared. A missing image or unavailable optional tool can have a different cause from an incorrect game record. If reloading does not help, report the exact page and the feature that failed, including your browser and the steps needed to reproduce it.'
WHERE `url` = 'faq' AND `locale` = 0 AND `rev` = 0 AND `editAccess` = 2
    AND `type` IS NULL AND `typeId` IS NULL
    AND SHA2(`article`, 256) = 'e707d03e7cdfc51ecec14328495a481adedd3626f048ad1a342a73c29c034c3e';

-- Replace only the bundled English What's New placeholder, preserving editorial overrides.
UPDATE `aowow_articles`
SET `article` = '[small]Website highlights — 23 October 2026[/small]\n\nRecent updates make it easier to explore the Wrath database, follow useful guides and get help when you need it. Here are the improvements you can use while planning your next quest, equipment upgrade or character build.\n\n[h2]Easier browsing on phones[/h2]\nDatabase pages, menus and contribution panels now fit smaller screens more comfortably. Wide tables scroll within their own area, helping you keep the rest of the page in view. Guide tables are easier to read, with clearer headings and better wrapping for longer descriptions.\n\nImages and maps also keep their place while loading, reducing the movement of nearby text as you read longer pages. Core entry information and ordinary links remain readable when interactive features are unavailable.\n\n[h2]Guides that connect the details[/h2]\nGuide categories now have clearer introductions and links to other topics with published guides. Related-guide links can also appear on database entries and guide pages, helping you move from an individual item, quest or NPC to a fuller explanation.\n\nGuides support tables for steps, requirements and locations, plus labelled map pins. Dungeon maps can show the relevant floor, making directions more useful when a location spans several levels. Pin labels and coordinates remain available as text when an interactive map cannot be shown.\n\n[h2]Item categories back in place[/h2]\nContainers, projectiles and quivers once again appear in their own browsing categories. This includes specialty bags, arrows and bullets, so you can look for storage or ammunition without finding those entries mixed into armor lists.\n\nThe shortcuts below take you straight to these categories.\n\n[h2]Festival guide fixes[/h2]\nSeveral festival guides now link to the correct event entries. The [url=?guide=lunar-festival]Lunar Festival guide[/url] is one of the corrected pages. [url=?guide=childrens-week]Children\'s Week[/url] and [url=?guide=midsummer-fire-festival]Midsummer[/url] also have their matching guide content restored.\n\nThese corrections make it easier to follow seasonal instructions and check the event details that belong to them.\n\n[h2]Clearer help and examples[/h2]\nThe About page now explains AoWoW, its Wrath focus and its history. The FAQ answers practical questions about finding records, planning builds, contributing and reporting problems.\n\nThe markup guide includes working table, map and tab examples alongside the formatting you can copy. Talent calculator help explains how to open shared builds and use supported older links. Other help pages have clearer contact links, and obsolete resource lists and broken forum links have been removed.\n\n[h2]Try the improvements[/h2]\n[table class=grid]\n[tr][td=header]What would you like to do?[/td][td=header]Start here[/td][/tr]\n[tr][td]Browse bags and ammunition[/td][td][url=?items=1]Containers[/url], [url=?items=6]projectiles[/url] and [url=?items=11]quivers[/url][/td][/tr]\n[tr][td]Find a useful walkthrough[/td][td][url=?guides]Browse guides[/url][/td][/tr]\n[tr][td]Check a location[/td][td][url=?maps]Explore maps[/url][/td][/tr]\n[tr][td]Understand character-building tools[/td][td][url=?help=talent-calculator]Talent calculator help[/url][/td][/tr]\n[tr][td]See formatting examples[/td][td][url=?help=markup-guide]Markup guide[/url][/td][/tr]\n[tr][td]Get answers or learn about the project[/td][td][url=?faq]Frequently asked questions[/url] and [url=?aboutus]About AoWoW[/url][/td][/tr]\n[/table]\n\nFound a detail that still needs attention? Use the Feedback option in the header or [url=?aboutus#contact]our contact form[/url]. Include the affected page and a short explanation of what you expected to find.'
WHERE `url` = 'whats-new' AND `locale` = 0 AND `rev` = 0 AND `editAccess` = 2
    AND `type` IS NULL AND `typeId` IS NULL
    AND SHA2(`article`, 256) = '761438607c0460181d6ac49a5cde748e45831be21b4e8ba293d908822859ab85';
